          <li><strong>FBI-Approved Channeler (Recommended):</strong> Use a channeler for 1&ndash;3 business day turnaround. Several channelers have Florida locations or can be used remotely. Find the approved list at fbi.gov.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct FBI Submission:</strong> If you prefer, submit directly to the FBI. Allow 8&ndash;14 weeks. Not recommended given the time constraints of the Miami appointment backlog.</li>
          <li><strong>US Department of State Apostille:</strong> Once you have your FBI result, mail to the State Dept. Authentications Office. Allow 6&ndash;8 weeks standard; expedited processing is available.</li>
          <li><strong>Sworn Spanish Translation:</strong> The apostilled FBI check needs a certified sworn Spanish translation.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="info-box tip">
          <strong>Start Your FBI Check on the Day You Book Your Appointment</strong>
          <p>Given Miami's 6&ndash;14 week appointment queue plus 8&ndash;12 weeks for FBI check with apostille, these processes can run in parallel if started simultaneously. Use a channeler and expedited apostille to compress the FBI check process to 4&ndash;6 weeks. Starting later risks your FBI check arriving after your appointment date, forcing a rescheduled submission.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>Spain-Compliant Health Insurance for Florida Applicants</h2>
        <p>Spain requires DNV applicants to hold health insurance with no copayments, valid in Spain for the full intended stay. Most Florida health plans &mdash; including Florida Blue (BCBS), Aetna, a leading private insurer domestic, Molina, Humana, and Medicare &mdash; do not qualify because they have deductibles and copayments or lack Spain coverage.</p>

        <p>You need a dedicated international or Spanish expat health policy. Suitable providers include a leading private insurer, a leading private insurer established private health insurers in Spain Care, a leading private insurer Global, and a leading private insurer. The key requirements:</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li>Coverage valid in Spain (territorial coverage explicitly stated)</li>
          <li>No copayments (the insurer pays 100% of covered costs)</li>
          <li>Minimum 12 months of coverage</li>
          <li>No exclusions or waiting periods affecting basic coverage</li>
          <li>Policy certificate available in Spanish or with sworn translation</li>
          <li>Policy is in your name (not a group or employer policy)</li>
        </ul>

        <p>See our <a href="/dnv-health-insurance/">comprehensive DNV health insurance guide</a> for a detailed comparison of compliant providers and what to look for when purchasing a policy.</p>

