          <li><strong>Finance and fintech:</strong> Miami has a large financial services sector; remote CFOs, analysts, compliance officers, and fintech professionals working for US or international firms all qualify</li>
          <li><strong>Real estate (advisory):</strong> Remote real estate consultants or analysts working for non-Spanish clients; note that actively transacting Spanish real estate requires different licensing</li>
          <li><strong>Creative industries:</strong> Miami&rsquo;s art, design, and media communities travel well; graphic designers, video producers, photographers, and content creators qualify if working for non-Spanish clients</li>
          <li><strong>Marketing and digital:</strong> Performance marketers, social media specialists, SEO/SEM professionals, content strategists</li>
          <li><strong>Healthcare technology:</strong> Telemedicine professionals, health tech product managers, medical writers for non-Spanish providers</li>
          <li><strong>Legal (US law):</strong> US-qualified lawyers advising non-Spanish clients on US or international law matters</li>
